### Lumie API Examples
### Compatible with IntelliJ HTTP Client and VS Code REST Client
### Replace {{host}} and {{token}} with actual values, or define in http-client.env.json

@host = http://localhost:8080
@token = <your-jwt-here>
@tenant = dev

### Auth — Login
POST {{host}}/v1/login
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Slug: {{tenant}}

{
  "loginId": "admin@lumie.kr",
  "password": "secret"
}

### Auth — Get active sessions
GET {{host}}/v1/me/sessions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Tenant-Slug: {{tenant}}

### Auth — Revoke all other sessions
DELETE {{host}}/v1/me/sessions?exclude=current
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Tenant-Slug: {{tenant}}

### Auth — Revoke single session
DELETE {{host}}/v1/me/sessions/{{sid}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Tenant-Slug: {{tenant}}

### Classes — List (paginated)
GET {{host}}/v1/classes?page=0&size=20&sort=createdAt,desc
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Tenant-Slug: {{tenant}}

### Students — List
GET {{host}}/v1/students?page=0&size=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Tenant-Slug: {{tenant}}

### Exams — List results
GET {{host}}/v1/exams/{{examId}}/results
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Tenant-Slug: {{tenant}}

### Exams — Update a single question answer (flat URL, replaces deep nested path)
PATCH {{host}}/v1/question-results/{{questionResultId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Tenant-Slug: {{tenant}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "selectedChoice": "3"
}

### Exams — Export results as CSV
GET {{host}}/v1/exams/results/export.csv
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Tenant-Slug: {{tenant}}
Accept: text/csv

### SMS — List templates
GET {{host}}/v1/sms-templates?page=0&size=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Tenant-Slug: {{tenant}}

### SMS — Create template
POST {{host}}/v1/sms-templates
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Tenant-Slug: {{tenant}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "입금 안내",
  "content": "[루미] 수강료 납부 안내입니다."
}

### Files — Upload (multipart)
POST {{host}}/v1/files/upload
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Tenant-Slug: {{tenant}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary

--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="homework.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ./homework.pdf
--boundary--
